1
00:00:03,337 --> 00:00:05,577
(Leonard:)I got to tell you, the more
I read about the primordial

2
00:00:05,739 --> 00:00:08,519
(Leonard:)gravity wave discovery,
the more excited I get.

3
00:00:08,675 --> 00:00:10,485
(Raj:)I know. Being an
astrophysicist right now

4
00:00:10,644 --> 00:00:11,744
(Raj:)is like being a rock star.

5
00:00:11,912 --> 00:00:13,552
(Howard:)Only without the sex.

6
00:00:15,082 --> 00:00:16,922
(Raj:)Yeah, literally, none of it.

7
00:00:18,585 --> 00:00:19,995
(Leonard:)What do you think about it, Sheldon?

8
00:00:20,153 --> 00:00:21,653
(Sheldon:)Meh.

9
00:00:21,822 --> 00:00:23,662
(Raj:)Are you kidding me?

10
00:00:23,824 --> 00:00:25,864
(Raj:)This may be the biggest
scientific breakthrough

11
00:00:26,026 --> 00:00:27,096
(Raj:)of our lifetime.

12
00:00:27,261 --> 00:00:30,611
(Raj:)How can you, as a theoretical
physicist, not care about this?

13
00:00:30,764 --> 00:00:32,744
(Sheldon:)Maybe it's because
I'm not an elitist.

14
00:00:34,268 --> 00:00:36,178
(Sheldon:)How does this gravity wave
breakthrough

15
00:00:36,336 --> 00:00:37,936
(Sheldon:)help the man on the street?
You know?

16
00:00:38,105 --> 00:00:39,885
(Sheldon:)Who's looking out
for Joe Six-Pack

17
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:42,420
(Sheldon:)and all his quantum physics concerns?

18
00:00:42,576 --> 00:00:45,216
(Leonard:)Oh, my God, you're jealous.

19
00:00:45,379 --> 00:00:47,289
(Sheldon:)Why would I be jealous?

20
00:00:47,447 --> 00:00:49,757
(Leonard:)I don't know. Maybe because
the origin of the universe

21
00:00:49,917 --> 00:00:52,587
(Leonard:)just got proven,
the Higgs field just got proven

22
00:00:52,753 --> 00:00:55,393
(Leonard:)and you've been working on
string theory for the last 20 years

23
00:00:55,556 --> 00:00:58,036
(Leonard:)and you're no closer to proving
it than when you started.

24
00:00:59,092 --> 00:01:02,022
(Sheldon:)Yeah, well, I've had a lot
on my plate.

